ame conditional guarded-hash construction in its finally block. A newly created file is therefore absent from the expected mapping unless verify_hashes has undocumented unexpected-file detection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"scripts/run_accounting_master.py\",\n      \"finding\": \"The worker-forgery requirement is stated as a tested interface, but the packet does not show a creation-after-absence case proving that requirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"tests/test_accounting_master.py\",\n      \"finding\": \"The supplied test names include test_worker_cannot_forge_supervisor_state, but no supplied assertion or code shows that the test covers creation of a previously absent state or authorization file.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"title\": \"New supervisor-control files may evade worker integrity verification\",\n      \"location\": \"scripts/run_accounting_master.py: Master.worker and Master._worker_result\",\n      \"problem\": \"The pre-worker guard records hashes only for files that already exist. If a worker creates state.json or authorization.json when absent, the post-worker verify_hashes call receives no expected entry for that path. Unless verify_hashes explicitly rejects unexpected files, the mutation is not detected and a worker can forge supervisor state or the upfront grant.\",\n      \"repair\": \"Make the guard represent both existence and digest, or explicitly compare the protected/control path set before and after execution. Reject any newly created supervisor-control file unless the controller itself authorized that creation. Apply the same rule in process-level cleanup where guarded controls are constructed conditionally. Add tests for creation of absent state.json and authorization.json during normal, malformed-response, and exception paths.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"residuals\": [\n    \"The packet does not provide verify_hashes or merge_hashes implementations, so their behavior for unexpected files is an unresolved interface assumption. If verify_hashes already rejects unlisted files, document and test that contract; otherwise the issue remains blocking.\",\n    \"The packet does not establish whether mcp list output is complete for every startup integration. The current code checks enabled flags for returned entries only; completeness should be documented or tested, but this is residual until the CLI-output contract is supplied.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_actions\": [\n    \"Inspect or specify verify_hashes semantics for absent and unexpected paths.\",\n    \"Add the missing creation-after-absence integrity tests before accepting the worker boundary.\",\n    \"Re-run the focused worker-boundary test set and retain the resulting evidence.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
